## Integrating Tailwind CSS with Nuxt 3

Nuxt 3 uses a powerful **module system** to extend its core functionality. For styling, the recommended approach for Tailwind CSS is to use the official **`@nuxtjs/tailwindcss`** module.

### Installation & Configuration

Integrating Tailwind is a two-step process:

1.  **Install the dependency**: Run the following command to add the module to your project's development dependencies.

    ```bash
    npm install --save-dev @nuxtjs/tailwindcss
    ```

2.  **Add to `nuxt.config.ts`**: Register the module in your Nuxt configuration file.

    ```javascript
    export default defineNuxtConfig({
      modules: [
        '@nuxtjs/tailwindcss'
      ]
    })
    ```

> [!NOTE]
> Once the module is added, you can immediately start using Tailwind's utility classes in your `.vue` files without any further configuration.

### Applying Utility Classes

After setup, you can add Tailwind classes directly to your HTML elements. For example, to style a header and navigation bar in a layout file (`layouts/default.vue`):

```html
<header class="shadow-sm bg-white">
  <nav class="container mx-auto p-4 flex justify-between">
    <a href="/" class="font-bold">Nuxt Dojo</a>
    <ul class="flex gap-4">
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</header>
```

- **`shadow-sm bg-white`**: Adds a small box-shadow and a white background.
- **`container mx-auto`**: Centers the content with a max-width.
- **`flex justify-between`**: Uses Flexbox to space out the child elements.

## Extending Tailwind CSS

You can extend Tailwind with your own custom styles or component classes by creating a specific file.

- **File Path**: Create a file at `assets/css/tailwind.css`.

- **File Contents**: The file must import Tailwind's layers. You can then add your own styles.

    ```css
    @tailwind base;
    @tailwind components;
    @tailwind utilities;

    /* Example: Apply a global background color */
    body {
      @apply bg-gray-50;
    }

    /* Example: Create a custom component class */
    @layer components {
      .btn {
        @apply bg-[#12b488] text-white px-3 py-2 rounded-md text-sm;
      }
    }
    ```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> When you create or modify the `assets/css/tailwind.css` file, you may need to **restart the Nuxt development server** for the changes to be detected and applied correctly.
